export const aboutMarkdown = `Nathan's AI is an interactive portfolio for Nathan Brodin, a frontend engineer. Instead of reading a static page, you can ask questions about his experience, projects, and the way he builds for the web. Answers stream back from a language model and can include links, sources, and short follow-up questions.

## How it works

Each message is sent to a chat endpoint, where a language model writes the reply. While answering, the model can use tools:

- **Web search** for current information beyond its training data.
- **Web fetch** to read a page and summarize it.
- **GitHub repository lookup** for public project stats such as stars, forks, open issues, and primary language.
- **Clarifying questions** when a request is ambiguous.

Replies stream token by token, so you can read them as they arrive. Completed conversations are saved and can be shared with a public link. See the [privacy page](/privacy) for what is stored and who processes it.

## What to ask

- Nathan's experience, roles, and the problems he works on.
- Projects, architecture, and the trade-offs behind them.
- The stack, tooling, and workflow he uses day to day.
- How he approaches performance, accessibility, and design systems.
- Whether he is available for work, and how to get in touch.

Answers reflect the model's interpretation of the context and tools available to it. For anything important, verify the details against the [portfolio](${siteConfig.portfolioUrl}), the [resume](${siteConfig.resumeUrl}), or by contacting Nathan directly.

## Who built it

Nathan's AI is designed, built, and maintained by [Nathan Brodin](${siteConfig.portfolioUrl}). He is a frontend engineer focused on fast, accessible product interfaces. You can find his work on the [portfolio](${siteConfig.portfolioUrl}) and his code on [GitHub](https://github.com/NathanBrodin).

## Technical stack

- **Framework:** TanStack Start with React and TypeScript, rendered on the server and hydrated in the browser.
- **UI:** Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui, with Cal Sans and Geist Mono.
- **AI:** Vercel AI SDK with OpenRouter as the model gateway for streaming, tool calls, and token usage.
- **Data:** PostgreSQL with Drizzle ORM. Conversations are stored as JSON message history with metadata.
- **Auth:** Better Auth with email and password, GitHub, or Google sign-in.
- **Rate limiting:** Upstash Redis.
- **Hosting:** Vercel.

## Source

The project is open source under the MIT license. Read the [Chat source code on GitHub](${siteConfig.githubUrl}), browse the [AI-readable site index](/llms.txt), or check the [privacy page](/privacy).

## Frequently asked questions

${faqMarkdown}
`

export const privacyMarkdown = `This page explains what Nathan's AI stores, who processes it, and what is public. It applies to the chat app at ${siteConfig.url}.

## Conversations are public

When a reply finishes, the conversation is saved with a random identifier. Each saved conversation has a public URL under \`/conversations\`, and the conversations index lists recent chats. Anyone with the link can read the full message history.

Conversations are marked noindex so search engines should not add them to their results, but that is not a privacy guarantee. Treat any conversation you save as public, and do not include passwords, API keys, private documents, or personal details you would not want others to read.

## What is stored

For each conversation, the app stores:

- a random identifier and a title derived from the first message;
- the full message history, including model replies and tool calls;
- token usage reported by the model;
- creation and update timestamps;
- approximate location, described below.

### Approximate location

The app reads Vercel's geolocation headers from each request. When available, it stores the city, country, region, latitude, longitude, and timezone associated with the request. Vercel derives these values from the IP address, so they are approximate and can be wrong. Outside Vercel, these fields are empty.

The IP address itself is not stored with the conversation. It is used for rate limiting as described below.

## Accounts

Signing in is optional. When you create an account, authentication is handled by Better Auth. Depending on how you sign in, the app stores your name, email address, profile image, and the identifiers needed to link a GitHub or Google account. Passwords for email sign-in are hashed by Better Auth before storage. Account records live in the same PostgreSQL database as conversations.

Questions about account data can be sent to [${siteConfig.email}](mailto:${siteConfig.email}).

## Cookies and local storage

- Session cookies set by Better Auth keep you signed in after you authenticate.
- The \`conversations_sidebar_open\` cookie remembers whether the conversation sidebar is open. It is httpOnly and expires after one year.
- Your theme preference is stored in your browser's local storage under the key \`theme\`. It is never sent to the server. A small inline script applies the saved theme before the page loads.

The app does not include advertising cookies or cross-site tracking scripts.

## Third parties

- **OpenRouter** receives your messages and returns the model's output. It routes requests to model providers under its own terms and privacy policy: https://openrouter.ai/privacy. Web search requests are also handled through OpenRouter.
- **Upstash Redis** stores rate-limit counters keyed by IP address. Each key expires when its window ends.
- **GitHub** receives public repository names when the model looks up repository stats.
- **Vercel** hosts the app and supplies the geolocation headers used for conversations.
- **Websites the model fetches** receive a request from the app when the model chooses to read a page.
- **GitHub and Google** receive authentication requests if you choose social sign-in.

## Rate limiting

To prevent abuse, \`/api/chat\` is limited per IP address: 5 requests in 30 seconds and 50 requests in 24 hours. The counters are stored in Upstash Redis and expire automatically. Requests over the limit are rejected with a retry time.

## Retention and contact

Conversations and account records remain stored until they are removed by the site operator. There is no self-service delete flow yet. For questions about this policy, stored data, or removal requests, email [${siteConfig.email}](mailto:${siteConfig.email}).
`
